node_modules/
dist/
build/
.env
server/.env
web/.env
*.log
*.log.[0-9]*
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
web/vite.config.js
web/vite.config.d.ts

# The local override holds the address of HCML's Zabbix: never commit it. Keep it out here, not only in one clone's
# .git/info/exclude, which a fresh clone or another machine does not have.
docker-compose.override.yml

# A downloaded SLA report names every device in the estate: never commit one.
HCML_SLA_Report_*

# Screenshots of the live portal show real host and site names: never commit them (docs/contributing.md).
/pic/

# What tools/live/api-timing.py writes where it is run.
api-timing.json

# What `npm test` writes in server/ and web/: how many tests ran, which tools/check/facts.check.mjs holds the documents' counts to.
.test-counts.json

# What `npm run test:coverage` writes in server/ and web/: the report of which lines the tests ran.
coverage/

# A copy or variant of a secret file, and the portal's state file (saved recipient addresses): never commit them.
.env.*
!.env.example
portal-state.json
*.bak

# The portal's users with their password hashes (users.json and its copies: .prev, .repaired-<time>, .broken-<time>), the web check figures of closed months and the requests for an
# account, which hold the names and reasons that strangers typed. A development run with PORTAL_STATE_DIR set writes them where it points, usually inside the repository: never commit them (SC-66, FR-62).
users.json*
closed-months.json*
requests.json*
*.broken-*

# Kept outside the repository, in a private folder: the work log (it holds every open weak point of HCML's systems and the owner's
# words), the first audit (run on a restore of HCML's production backup), the two handbook pages that list what is still open, and the
# dated change logs of October. On the machine of the owner `tracker.md` is a link to the private copy, so the checks that read it still run;
# a fresh clone has none of them, and the checks accept that.
/tracker.md
/AUDIT_REPORT.md
/docs/handover/5-reference/open-items.md
/docs/handover/5-reference/open-problems.md
/docs/handover/0-everyone/risks-limits-costs.md

# Pictures kept outside the repository: the screenshots of the main pages (their counts, site names and host group names are real) and the PNG renders of the ERD diagrams,
# which the .mmd sources and the PDFs next to them can make again.
/docs/screenshots/
/docs/erd/**/*.png
/docs/setup/[34][0-9]-what-changed-*.md

# A dump of a database, an encrypted copy, a token, a key or a certificate: never commit one. A copy of the production Zabbix, a backup of
# the portal's state and the files that deploy/backup-state.sh makes belong outside the repository.
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump
*.enc
*.token
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

